      "id": "msiqb4g",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "C. Chemical Weathering Processes"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Oxidation – reaction with oxygen (iron-rich rocks).",
      "id": "09i2ltb"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Carbonation – carbonic acid dissolves limestone (karst landscapes).",
      "id": "qwve908"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Hydrolysis – formation of clay minerals.",
      "id": "mk1asta"
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Feature",
        "Mechanical Weathering",
        "Chemical Weathering"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Primary Process",
          "Physical disintegration without altering mineral composition",
          "Decomposition accompanied by chemical changes in rock minerals"
        ],
        [
          "Key Examples",
          "Freeze-Thaw, Exfoliation, Salt Crystallization, Unloading",
          "Oxidation, Carbonation, Hydrolysis, Hydration, Solution"
        ],
        [
          "Resulting Products",
          "Smaller rock fragments, block and granular debris",
          "Clay minerals, dissolved ions, altered rock faces (e.g., karst)"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "xsrqzyf"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Hydration – absorption of water causing expansion.",
      "id": "pjgixkr"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Solution – complete dissolution of soluble minerals.",
      "id": "falwqgg"
    },
    {
      "id": "6p6vqyl",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "D. Special Forms of Weathering"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Spheroidal Weathering – rounded rock forms due to chemical attack at corners.",
      "id": "9aoo7xf"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Laterization – intense leaching in tropical climates forming laterite soils.",
      "id": "t5ayxbw"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Differential Weathering – softer rocks weather faster than hard rocks.",
      "id": "8gbodly"
    },
    {
