      "content": "• Climate (temperature &amp; rainfall)",
      "id": "uvlvkm4"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Weathering is an 'in-situ' process—meaning no movement or transportation takes place, distinguishing it from erosion.",
        "Carbonation action on limestone produces karst landscapes, a frequent topic in competitive geography exams.",
        "Hydrolysis specifically leads to the formation of clay minerals.",
        "Laterization is associated with intense leaching under tropical climate conditions."
      ],
      "id": "l2d7xjo"
